  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;be any two <math> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;matrices. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is symmetric and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is skew symmetric, then the matrix&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "skew symmetric",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math>&nbsp;is an identity matrix",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "&nbsp;symmetric",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "neither symmetric nor skew symmetric",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A square matrix <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is said to be a symmetric matrix, if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;and it&nbsp;is said to be a skew symmetric matrix, if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>T</mi></msup></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></math></p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;a symmetric matrix.</p>"
  }
}